                "text_b3NQiJ": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "enable_strikethrough": false,
                    "enable_custom_text_color": true,
                    "custom_text_color": "#b9b5ad",
                    "text": "<p><em>Every kitchen asks one question. For us, it was: what should a cook's knife collection actually do? A single blade had always been the answer — one knife, every task, every compromise. We asked for three.</em></p><p><em>Bringing three knives to one set meant holding the same standard across every blade. Each knife is shaped and forged by hand, its hammered surface left in the texture of the forge rather than polished away. The edge is ground to a clean, confident bite, and the rosewood handle — fixed with solid brass rivets — sits balanced in the hand. Hand-forged is rough. A daily knife must be steady. Making both hold in one grip is the challenge this set was built to answer.</em></p><p><em>The result is a set that covers a full day of prep — chopping, firmer cuts and fine detail — balanced to feel natural in the hand, yet ready for real work. Three blades, one forged standard: a kitchen set made to be reached for, again and again.</em></p>",
                    "collection_description_only": false,
